<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ishpabara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 708–702 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ishpabara was a king of Ellipi in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> in the late 8th century BCE, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalta">Dalta</a>. When his father died in 708 BCE he fought his brother Nibe for the throne and was installed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a>'s Assyrian troops, while Nibe's Elamite allies were driven off. He later turned against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>, and in 702 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sennacherib">Sennacherib</a> sacked his royal city, Marubishtu, and annexed part of his kingdom.</p></div>
